div0.entryFree:
δαί, colloquial form ofδή,used after interrogatives, to express wonder or curiosity,
τίς δ. ὅμιλος ὅδ' ἔπλετο;
Od. 1.225
; ποῦ δ. νηῦς ἕστηκε;
24.299
, cf. A.D. Synt. 78.2 (but wrongly read by Aristarch. for δ' αἱ
Il. 10.408
): freq. in Com., τί δ. σὺ . . πεποίηκας;
Ar. Eq. 351
; mostly in a separate clause, τίδ.;
what? how?
Pherecr. 93
, Ar. Eq. 171 , al.; τί δ. σύ;
Id. Av. 136
; πῶς δ.;
Id. V. 1212
; dub. l. in A. Pr. 933 , Ch. 900 , S. Ant. 318 , but prob. to be read E. Med. 1012 , Ion 275 , al.: freq. in codd. of Pl. , but prob. f.l. for δέ , as in Ar. Ach. 912 .

δαιμονιώδης,ες,
like a demon,Sch. Ar. Ra. 293 ;
demoniacal, devilish,
Ep.Jac. 3.15 ;
like a δαίμων,
Procl. in Ti. 1.113D.

δαίτηθεν,Adv.
from a feast,
Od. 10.216 , Theoc. 17.28 .

δείδεκτο,δειδέχαται,δειδέχατο,

    v.
    δειδίσκομαι;

δημοθοιν-ία,ἡ,
public feast,
Arist. Mu. 400b21 (pl.), Luc. Dem. Enc. 16 , CIG 2880 (Branchidae), Ph. 2.55 , OGI 533.9 (Ancyra):— Delph.δᾱμο-, SIG 672.53 .

δήποθεν, indef.Adv.(better writtenδή ποθεν)
from any quarter,
Pl. Ep. 331e ; dub. l. in A. Ch. 632 (lyr.); perh. = δήπου , as in Orac. ap. Phleg. Olymp.Fr. 1 , Iamb. Myst. 5.20 .

διαβροχή,ἡ,
maceration, v.l. in Dsc. 2.107 , cf. Antyll. ap. Orib. 4.11.2 ;
soaking, wetting, σωμάτωνib. 9.23.1 .

διᾰναγκ-ασμός,ὁ,=foreg.;
machine for this purpose,
Id. Art. 47 .

διά-πτωμα,ατος,τό,
stumble, slip,
Philem. 60 ;
error,
Chrysipp.Stoic. 2.215 , Phld. Herc. 1251.5 ;
failure,opp.ἐπίτευγμα,
Id. Po. 5.21 ;μεγάλοις δ. περιπίπτεινfall in with great
losses, IPE 12.32.55 (Olbia), cf. SIG 364.62 (Ephesus);
loss, deficiencyin accounts, PHib. 1.52.9
(iii B.C.), etc.

δῐαυλοδρομ-έω,
to run the δίαυλος,Sch. Ar. Av. 293 ;
return to the starting-point,
Arist. GA 741b21 ; of the moon, Ph. 1.24 ; of evils,
recur,
Id. 2.350 .

δί-μορφος[ῐ],ον,
two-formed,
Lyc. 111 , 892 ;
of twin form,Vett. Val. 13.3 ;
androgynous,
D.S. 32.12 .

διοτιδήποτε,
for whatever reason,
Simp. in Ph. 50.20 .

δῐ́χο-θεν,Adv.
from both sides, both ways,
A. Pers. 76 (lyr.), Ar. Pax 477 , Th. 2.44 , etc.; δ. μισθοφορεῖν
D. 24.123
;
from two sources,
τὸ δίκαιον δ. συνίσταται
Aps. Rh. p.294H.

δῠσ-άερος[ᾱ],ον ,
having bad air,δεσμωτήριον(sc.ὁ κόσμος) D.Chr. 30.11 ;
unwholesome, of the atmosphere, Procl. Par.Ptol. 122 , cf. Sabin. ap. Orib. 9.20.8 .

δῠσαπό-βλητος,ον,
hard to get rid of, πυρετός
Alex.Aphr. Febr. 19
;
hard to cast away, Olymp. in Alc. p.51 C.;
hard to lose, Id. in Cat. 116.25 , cf. Ammon. in Cat. 82.8 , Simp. in Cat. 228.23 .

δῠσ-αφαίρετος,ον,
hard to take away, Arist. EN 1095b26 ;
hard to remove, of an application, Gal. 12.356 .

δῠσέργ-εια,ἡ,
difficulty, Sor. 2.53 , Orib. 45.18.14 ;
functional defect, Paul.Aeg. 6.42 , al.

δῠσεργ-ία,ἡ,
difficulty in workingor
construction, δυσεργίαν παρέχειν
Ph. Bel. 56.42
, cf. Hero Aut. 23.8 (in form -έργεια), Plu. Aem. 16 ;
difficultyin pronouncing, ἡ ἐν τῇ προφορᾷ δ.
Phld. Po. 2.42
;
inability to exert oneself, Hp. VM 10 ( v.l. δυσοργίη );
inability to act, App. Syr. 19 .

δῠσ-έψητος,ον,=foreg., Phryn. PS p.33
B. ;
hard to cook, Gal. 6.541 ( Comp. ).

δῠσηκο-ί̈α,ἡ,
hardness of hearing, Dsc. 5.17 , Plu. 2.1073d , Vett.Val. 109.31 ;
disobedience, Plu. 2.794d .

δυσκατα-πόνητος,ον,
hard to execute, M.Ant. 6.19 , Arr. Epict. 3.12.8 ;
hard to digest, Sor. 2.32 .

δύσ-ληπτος,ον,
hard to take hold of, Sor. 1.88 ;
hard to catch, μοχθηρία
Ph. 2.366
, cf. Luc. Anach. 27 ;
hard to comprehend, Str. 13.4.12 , A.D. Synt. 225.28 , Plu. 2.17d .

δυσπαράγρᾰφος,ον,
hard to define, ποσότης
Plb. 16.12.10
;
hard to state precisely, Id. 18.15.1 ;
hard to terminate, of life, Phld. Herc. 1251.16 .

δύσ-φθαρτος,ον,
hard to destroy, S.E. M. 9.19 ;
not easily spoilt, Diph.Siph. ap. Ath. 3.121c , Hices.ib. 87d , Xenocr. 73 ( Comp. ), Dsc. 2.9 .

δυσχέρ-ασμα,ατος,τό, in pl.,
harsh judgements, Pl. Phlb. 44d ;
inconveniences, Dam. Isid. 66 :—condemned by Poll. 3.133 .

δῠσωπ-ία,ἡ,
confusion of face, shamefacedness, Phld. Lib. p.24 O., Ph. 2.603 (pl.), Plu. 2.95b ;
false modesty, ib. 528e , al.;
cause for shame, ib. 707e , Cic. Att. 13.33.2 ;δυσωπίαν
habere, to have
an ugly look, ib. 16.15.2 ;τὰς δ.( v.l. δυστροπίας )τὰς ἐν τοῖς διαπορηθεῖσιdub. in Ph. 1.330 .

δωδεκᾰτημόριον,τό,
twelfth part, [χώρας] Pl. Lg. 848c , cf. IG 12(7).237.56 (Amorgos,ii/i B. C.), Ph. 1.673 ;
sign of the zodiac, Hipparch. 2.1.7 , Ptol. Tetr. 93 , etc.

δωρο-φόρος,ον,
bringing presents, Pi. P. 5.86 ,f.l. inEpigr. ap. Ath. 5.209e (Archimelos);
tributary, Euph. 78 .
